  "@id": "https://w3id.org/pices/odis/records/zenodo-23505385.jsonld",
  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Low-temperature Incubation of Walleye Pollock Eggs (Theragra chalcogramma) from the Southeast Bering Sea Region",
  "description": "Temperature-specific development rates of southeastern Bering Sea walleye Pollock eggs incubated at low temperatures (-0.6 to 3.8 C) to incorporate with similar data from the nearby Shelikof Strait area (Blood et al. 1994) in order to construct a model of temperature-specific development rates for walleye Pollock eggs over a broad range of temperatures (-0.6 to 7.7 C)\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To provide information for modelers to incorporate into biophysical models of ecosystem and IBM models",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23505386",
